id: pm-gh1662
title: "GH-1662: an infeasible --token-budget on context --for orient exits 0 with no context and contradictory receipts, its restore_with retry fails, and get/list intent receipts undercount the emitted envelope"
description: "GitHub issue #1662 (reported 2026-11-04 against 2026.11.4 from an agent-UX audit). Reproduced 2026-11-05 on the installed 2026.11.4 CLI in a disposable sandbox tracker holding one claimed Task with a linked file, doc and test. (1) pm context --for orient --token-budget 600 --json exits 0 with no context. The envelope (1,421 B, about 356 tokens) carries budget_exceeded with omitted_result true and reason effective_budget_infeasible, and context_intent says within_budget false and result_omitted true, yet read_output in the same envelope says within_budget true and result_omitted false. The same value spelled canonically, --output-budget 600, exits 2 with output_budget_exceeded, so the compatibility alias and the canonical flag disagree on success. The reporter reproduced the contradiction through the SDK with client.context({for: 'orient', tokenBudget: '600'}). (2) The advertised restore_with, pm context --for orient --token-budget 700 --limit 1, exits 2 with output_budget_exceeded (744 B), so following the envelope's own recovery is a retry that still yields no context. (3) pm get <id> --for inspect --token-budget 500 --json emits 2,149 B (about 538 tokens) while context_intent claims estimated_tokens 385 and within_budget true, and pm list --for triage --token-budget 500 --limit 2 --json emits 2,115 B (about 529 tokens) while claiming 376. Both exceed the budget they report fitting, because the intent receipt and the surrounding envelope are not part of the estimate. Expected: one budget contract for canonical and legacy spellings, an omitted required result is unambiguously unsuccessful (non-zero exit, every receipt agrees), the estimate covers the complete serialized envelope including receipts, and a suggested retry is verified against the same estimator. Why it matters for agents: a shell agent proceeds after exit 0 with no project context, an SDK consumer reading the shared read_output receipt reaches the same wrong conclusion, and the supplied recovery spends another call for nothing. This escapes closed acceptance criteria in the same family: pm-yekkvt AC3 (a response that omits its result never reports within_budget true), pm-3crymx AC3 (recovery guidance is verified to work on the corpus that produced the refusal), pm-xam9bt AC4 and AC7 (recovery bindings are executed for legacy budgets and repeated recovery makes progress without cycles), pm-8kzfc4 AC4 (canonical alias migration stays equivalent independently of token limits) and pm-7hbfch AC3 (the envelope carries a measured estimate so a consumer can detect an overrun without measuring bytes). Duplicate check: searched intent budget, receipt, omitted result, restore_with, legacy alias and estimator terms across all statuses, and no open item owns this. The report excludes GH-1428, GH-1552 and GH-1361 as separate subjects."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: agent-ux,context,"gh:1662",sdk,token-budget,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-11-05T06:08:49.535Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-07T04:59:17.249Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-07T04:18:19.912Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-07T04:18:19.912Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "pm context --for orient with a budget below its smallest feasible projection exits non-zero whether the budget is spelled --token-budget or --output-budget, in CLI, SDK and MCP, and every receipt in the envelope (budget_exceeded, context_intent and read_output) reports result_omitted true and within_budget false; The canonical --output-budget and the legacy --token-budget alias produce the same success, omission and exit status for the same value on the same corpus, proven by a spec that runs both spellings in JSON and TOON; Every restore_with or suggested retry an omission emits is executed by a spec against the same corpus and estimator and returns the requested result, or the envelope names an honest non-numeric alternative instead of a budget that cannot fit; The estimated_tokens that context_intent and read_output report for get --for inspect and list --for triage is computed over the complete serialized envelope including the receipts, and a spec asserts it is at least ceil(emitted UTF-8 bytes / 4) and that within_budget is false whenever the emitted output exceeds the budget; Negative control: reintroducing the intent-only estimate, or exit 0 on an omitted orient result, fails the specs above"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
repro_steps: "In a fresh tracker with one claimed Task: pm context --for orient --token-budget 600 --json (exit 0, no context, contradictory receipts). pm context --for orient --output-budget 600 --json (exit 2). Run the emitted restore_with with --json (exit 2). pm get <id> --for inspect --token-budget 500 --json and pm list --for triage --token-budget 500 --limit 2 --json (receipt estimate below the emitted size)"
resolution: "Intent reads now have one budget contract. The intent estimate measures the delivered encoding, without an unrequested row_contract, and is settled over the complete envelope including the read_output receipt. A numeric --output-budget binds the intent budget exactly like --token-budget, in both the SDK and the CLI global flag. A settled envelope over its intent budget is decided again with the measured overhead charged, and is omitted only when it still cannot fit. Every omitted result exits 2, and context_intent, read_output and the omission branch all agree. --output-include and continuation pages never strip a refusal. The legacy restore_with carries the 25% recovery margin and the caller's --fields, so the retry it names returns the result. The new SDK export isReadResultOmittedForBudget detects both branches."
expected_result: "Both budget spellings give the same outcome on the same corpus, an omitted result exits 2 with agreeing receipts, restore_with succeeds when executed, and intent receipts cover the emitted envelope"
actual_result: "Integration specs: spelling matrix 300/600/900/3000 in JSON and TOON; an executed restore_with returning the result; get/list estimates at or above the emitted size; a shaped get refusal exiting 2; agreeing continuation refusals; an exact session charge. Unit sweeps assert fit-or-exit-2. Calibration re-approved (session orientation 9,945 -> 8,210 tokens); token-budget gate requires exit 2 for the infeasible control; agent-task baseline +1 token"
affected_version: 2026.11.4
component: context
