comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T20:10:03.803Z","harness:claude-code","Root causes, reproduced on main af6fd5583 in a sandbox tracker with one claimed Task: (1) the intent estimate measured compact JSON of the projection whatever the delivered encoding, including a row_contract the host strips unless --output-row-contract is requested; pretty JSON was undercounted (get 381 vs 534 emitted, list 375 vs 528) and TOON overcounted, so --token-budget 600 omitted in TOON where --output-budget 600 succeeded. (2) A numeric --output-budget never bound the intent budget, so legacy derived a 1-row limit while canonical kept the declared 3000 ceiling (500 TOON: legacy exit 0, canonical exit 2; 5000 JSON: 988 vs 883 tokens). (3) An omitted intent result (budget_exceeded) never set the exit code, and the read_output receipt attached to it said within_budget true and result_omitted false. (4) restore_with used ceil(estimate/100)*100, so the retry sat at the edge of its own budget. Fix: updateContextIntentEstimate measures through estimateReadOutputTokens in the delivered encoding (the CLI's delivered renderer) and excludes an unrequested row_contract; a numeric canonical --output-budget becomes the intent's effective budget (row derivation, compaction, echo) through both SDK options and the CLI global flag, a canonical omission keeps the shared output_budget_exceeded branch, and --output-budget unbounded never omits; read_output inherits result_omitted from an omitted intent; the CLI exits 2 on isReadResultOmittedForBudget (new SDK export covering both branches); restore_with uses resolveReadOutputRecoveryBudget's 25% margin. Measured after the fix on the same corpus: for 300/500/600/900/1000/3000/5000 in JSON and TOON both spellings give identical exit codes and token counts; the emitted restore_with (pm context --for orient --token-budget 1100 --limit 1) exits 0 with the result. SDK and MCP at 300: every receipt reports result_omitted true; MCP keeps isError unset for budget omissions, as it already does for the canonical refusal."
  "2026-11-06T20:33:01.699Z","harness:claude-code","Calibration review: measuring the intent in the delivered encoding moved scripts/release/context-intent-calibration.json at the 2,243-item tier only. list delivers 69 rows in 3,162 tokens (was 67 in 3,080) against its 3,200 declaration, next 9 rows in 1,136 (was 8 in 1,053) against 1,200, search 28 rows in 1,766 (was 27 in 1,716) against 1,800. The session orientation sees 111 items in 9,945 of 20,000 tokens (was 107 in 9,687), and the list/search cursor walks need one and three fewer pages. Every intent still fits its declared ceiling; the compact-JSON estimate had been trimming rows the delivered TOON had room for. Approved with pnpm context:intent:calibrate --update."
  "2026-11-07T02:03:14.334Z","harness:claude-code","Codex batch review round 2 (P2), confirmed and fixed. Measuring the delivered encoding (and, under GH-1678, a custom renderer) removed the convergence guarantee the compact-JSON-only intent estimate had. A deterministic renderer that prints a remainder derived from context_intent.estimated_tokens makes the fixpoint in updateContextIntentEstimate alternate between 200 and 201 forever, so formatOutput never returned. The loop is now bounded by the shared MAX_ESTIMATE_ITERATIONS (8, the same bound the read_output receipt uses). On non-convergence it falls back to the largest estimate observed, so an oscillating receipt never understates within its cycle. Regression: delivered-output-budget.spec.ts 'terminates an intent estimate that a renderer makes oscillate' returns, with estimated_tokens >= the delivered tokens. Negative control: with the unbounded for(;;) loop restored the spec hangs until the 60 s harness timeout (exit 124). Converging inputs are unaffected; the calibration gate is unchanged."
  "2026-11-07T02:33:06.498Z","harness:claude-code","Codex batch review round 4 (P2), confirmed. The fix covers a wider defect than reported. attachReadOutputContracts settled receipts over the final envelope only on the suppressed-row-contract path. With --output-row-contract requested (or for results without a row_contract key) the intent receipt kept its pre-envelope estimate: 278 tokens for a 412-token delivery. A stable custom renderer was then needlessly sent through the round-3 native fallback. The intent decision itself also ignored the read_output receipt and the requested row contract, so the legacy spelling delivered over its budget with exit 0. Probe: list --for triage --token-budget 400 --output-row-contract delivered 445 tokens, while --output-budget 400 omitted with exit 2; get --for inspect at 700 delivered 705. Fix (src/sdk/context-intent-contracts.ts): attachReadOutputContracts is split into finalizeReadOutputEnvelope, which settles every intent result's receipts over the delivered envelope on every path, and settledIntentOmission. When a delivered, non-unbounded intent read's settled envelope exceeds its intent budget, settledIntentOmission decides it again through intentBudgetOutcome: the legacy budget_exceeded branch with a restore_with from the settled size, or the canonical output_budget_exceeded branch. The omission passes through the read-output stage again, so every receipt agrees and the CLI exits 2. Re-probe: no read under either spelling delivers over its budget. The one remaining boundary difference (get --output-row-contract at 700: legacy omits at 705, canonical fits at 692) is the legacy receipt's migration-hint bytes; docs/READ_OUTPUT_CONTRACTS.md now says so. Regressions in delivered-output-budget.spec.ts: settled native and stable-custom intent receipts with row contracts, the legacy and canonical omission at 400, the named retry budget returning the result, and unbounded keeping its result. Negative control: with the recheck disabled the legacy read exits 0 (expected undefined to be 2)."
  "2026-11-07T02:40:21.983Z","harness:claude-code","Round 4 follow-up: omitting a settled over-budget intent read was too harsh. In the calibration gate's 2,243-item session orientation, the read_session and read_output receipts pushed list, search and next past their per-call intent budgets, and those reads had been delivered over budget while claiming within_budget: true. The omission removed them entirely, so later reads suppressed nothing ('orientation session did not suppress repeated item facts'). The recheck is now a second pass instead. settledIntentOverhead measures how far the settled envelope exceeds the intent estimate. attachContextIntentReceipt then charges that overhead against its fit ceiling (keyed through a WeakMap on the second pass's options, invisible to callers), so row and recursive compaction leave room for the receipts. The receipt still reports the caller's budget. A read is omitted only when even its smallest projection cannot fit, and the legacy restore_with then sizes its retry from the complete envelope (intent estimate + overhead). Re-probe: list and get, with and without --output-row-contract, at 300/400/500/700 give identical exit codes and outcomes under --token-budget and --output-budget, and none delivers over budget. The calibration report was re-approved. The only change is the 2,243-tier session_orientation: spent 9,945 -> 8,210 tokens, seen items 111 -> 83, delivered bytes 39,771 -> 32,834, suppressed repeats unchanged at 8. Each session read now fits its own intent budget over its complete envelope."
  "2026-11-07T03:02:12.858Z","harness:claude-code","Codex batch review round 5: two P2s, both confirmed and fixed. (1) Include projection erased intent refusals. 'pm get <id> --for inspect --output-budget 300 --output-include item --json' returned item: {} with exit 0, because applyIncludeProjection treated output_budget_exceeded and context_intent as unselected sections, so read_output and isReadResultOmittedForBudget reported success. projectReadOutputRows now shapes only results that are not budget omissions (includeProjectionApplies in src/sdk/read-output-contracts.ts). Regression: the integration spec runs that exact CLI invocation from source and expects exit 2 with an omission. Negative control: without the guard it fails. (2) Reserving the measured overhead did not guarantee the re-settled second pass fits. A structured output_format service for next --for execute --token-budget 344 --output-row-contract delivered 345 tokens with exit 0. attachReadOutputContracts now rechecks the re-settled envelope (settledIntentOverBudget). A read still over its intent budget is omitted through intentBudgetOutcome, with restore_with sized from the settled envelope, and that omission passes through the read-output stage. Regression: a budget sweep 300..460 asserts that every read either fits its budget or is omitted with exit 2. Negative control: without the recheck it fails at 'budget 344: expected 345 to be less than or equal to 344'. docs/READ_OUTPUT_CONTRACTS.md states both rules."
  "2026-11-07T03:20:30.999Z","harness:claude-code","Codex batch review round 6: four P2s, all fixed (src/sdk/context-intent-contracts.ts, src/sdk/read-output-contracts.ts). (1) A successful --output-include projection removed context_intent, so both settled-budget checks were bypassed: 'get --for inspect --fields id,title,description,children --output-include item --token-budget 350 --output-row-contract' delivered 413 tokens with exit 0. settledIntentOverBudget now falls back to the first-pass intent receipt and measures the delivered envelope itself. Negative control: without the fallback the budget sweep fails. (2) collapseContinuationMetadata removed the intent receipt from refused continuation pages, so output_budget_exceeded shipped beside read_output.result_omitted false. An omission is no longer collapsed, and the read_output receipt recognizes either omission discriminator (isReadResultOmittedForBudget). (3) The legacy restore_with dropped --fields, so its retry requested far more data than the named budget allowed and refused again. buildContextIntentRecoveryCommand now carries the caller's --fields. Negative control: without it the executed retry fails. (4) Flipping within_budget after stabilization added an unmeasured byte, so the session under-charged by 1. reconcileIntentFit now runs inside the stabilization loop, so the flag settles with the estimates. With the TT fixture the intent stage already reports within_budget false, so the reorder is a structural guarantee: the exact-charge assertion (560 delivered, 560 estimated, next_state 575 = 15 + 560) holds. Regression: tests/integration/read-output/delivered-output-budget.integration.spec.ts 'binds include-shaped reads, keeps resumed refusals whole, names working retries and charges sessions exactly'. Convergence note: rounds 1-6 found 1, 2, 3, 1, 2 and 4 P2s. Each round mostly found compositions created by the previous round's guards."
  "2026-11-07T03:51:25.963Z","harness:claude-code","Static-gate findings on the final tree, fixed. (1) scripts/release/token-budget-gate.mjs ran its infeasible-intent negative control ('list --for triage --token-budget 256 --json') through runCliJson, which treats any non-zero exit as a crash. This batch makes an omitted intent result exit 2, so the gate died before reading the receipt. The control now runs with allowFailure, reads the receipt from the failed run, and additionally requires exit_status 2. The spec mock returns 2 for that read, and a new case fails when an omission exits 0. (2) Round 4's settling had started re-estimating omission envelopes, so an omitted result's context_intent.estimated_tokens reported the refusal's own size (203) instead of the omitted result's size (> 256). The receipt then said within_budget false at 203 <= 256. stabilizeSuppressedRowContractReceipts no longer re-estimates the intent receipt of an omitted result; the read_output receipt already measures the delivered envelope exactly. Token budget gate: passed (32 surfaces; infeasible effective intent receipt verified). Calibration gate: passed."
  "2026-11-07T04:50:47.230Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 7 on PR 1681 (P2, an ordinary caller), confirmed and fixed. 'pm get <id> --fields id,title --for inspect --token-budget 300 --output-row-contract --json' exited 2, but its intent receipt reported 205-210 tokens against a 300-token budget. The settled second pass reserved envelopeOverhead to decide fit, then restored the public budget without adding that overhead to the omitted result's estimate, and stabilization deliberately leaves omitted estimates alone. attachContextIntentReceipt now adds the reserved overhead to an omitted result's estimate, so the published omission explains itself (estimate > budget). Regression: the integration spec runs that exact invocation. Negative control: without the fix it fails with 'expected 205 to be greater than 300'. Token-budget, calibration and agent-task gates pass unchanged."
  "2026-11-07T04:59:17.249Z","harness:claude-code","Greptile review on PR 1681 (4/5). Finding 2 duplicates Codex round 7 and was fixed in the previous commit. Finding 1 was confirmed and fixed: a canonical intent refusal built by intentBudgetOutcome has no read_output receipt, and with no session, row contract or include selection, applyReadOutputDimensions' canReturnReadOutputUnchanged returned it before attaching one. isReadOutputBudgetExceeded still typed it as PmReadOutputBudgetExceeded, which promises read_output, so SDK callers reading read_output.estimated_tokens threw. canReturnReadOutputUnchanged now never short-circuits a budget omission. Regression: the integration spec scans SDK get --for inspect budgets to the first refusal and reads its read_output estimate. Negative control: without the guard it throws 'Cannot read properties of undefined (reading estimated_tokens)'. Token-budget, calibration and agent-task gates and the SDK surface and contract snapshots pass unchanged."
